DATA SOURCES

This server holds no legal corpus. Every answer is fetched at call time from a
keyless public Australian source and is attributed in the response itself.

Commonwealth legislation
  Federal Register of Legislation — https://www.legislation.gov.au/
  Material on the Register is published by the Office of Parliamentary Counsel
  under a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0),
  except for the Commonwealth Coat of Arms and any third-party material.
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  This server retrieves that material unmodified and identifies the compilation
  and register id it came from. Where the Register records that commenced
  amendments are not yet incorporated, the response says so.

Case law
  NSW Caselaw — https://www.caselaw.nsw.gov.au/ (Department of Communities and
    Justice, NSW)
  High Court of Australia — https://www.hcourt.gov.au/
  Queensland Judgments — https://www.queenslandjudgments.com.au/ (Incorporated
    Council of Law Reporting for Queensland)

State and Territory legislation
  Queensland — https://www.legislation.qld.gov.au/
  Tasmania — https://www.legislation.tas.gov.au/
  Western Australia — https://www.legislation.wa.gov.au/
  Victoria — https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/
  Northern Territory — https://legislation.nt.gov.au/
  Australian Capital Territory — https://www.legislation.act.gov.au/

Tribunals, regulators and registers
  Australian Taxation Office Legal Database — https://www.ato.gov.au/law/
  Fair Work Commission — https://www.fwc.gov.au/
  Office of the Australian Information Commissioner — https://www.oaic.gov.au/
  National Anti-Corruption Commission — https://www.nacc.gov.au/
  Merit Protection Commissioner — https://www.mpc.gov.au/
  Anti-Dumping Review Panel — https://www.industry.gov.au/
  Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade, Australian Treaties Database —
    https://docs.dfat.gov.au/
  Parliament of Australia and ParlInfo — https://www.aph.gov.au/,
    https://parlinfo.aph.gov.au/
  State Library of NSW legal glossary — https://legalanswers.sl.nsw.gov.au/

Each source's own terms of use govern the material it returns. Copyright in
Australian judgments and in State and Territory legislation is held by the
relevant Crown or reporting body; this server retrieves and reformats, it does
not relicense.

================================================================================

SOURCES THIS SERVER DOES NOT FETCH

These hosts are listed in `src/lib/upstream-hosts.ts` with `blocked: true`.
The server builds deep links to them and never requests them:

  AustLII and LawCite — https://www.austlii.edu.au/, https://lawcite.austlii.edu.au/
    Cloudflare-gated, and AustLII asks automated clients to contact it first.
  Federal Court of Australia — https://www.judgments.fedcourt.gov.au/
    Cloudflare challenge on every request.
  NSW legislation — https://legislation.nsw.gov.au/
  SA legislation — https://www.legislation.sa.gov.au/
    No public query surface; both registers discourage automated access.
  ACCC and the Australian Competition Tribunal — https://www.accc.gov.au/
    403 to non-browser clients.
  Commonwealth Ombudsman — https://www.ombudsman.gov.au/
    Cloudflare-gated.

A blocked source is reported as `[UPSTREAM_BLOCKED]` with a link. It is never
reported as an absence of the material.

